=== Findings ===
candidate_ids: skb.candidate_ids exists directly; used (not
get_candidate_ids()). Cardinality 129375, dense integer range 0..129374
(size == max+1, i.e. contiguous).

query_id vs subscript index: they DO NOT coincide once a real split is
selected (get_subset('val')/get_subset('test')) — every one of the 10
rows checked across both splits has row_query_id != idx. query_id is a
global id into the full un-split dataset (2241 val rows, 2801 test
rows, ids drawn from the full ~10k-query pool), not a per-split
sequential counter. score_one.py's load_split() already resolves by
the row's own query_id field via a full-dataset linear scan, never by
trusting a positional index — this probe confirms that was the
correct, necessary choice (RESEARCH Open Question 3 / Assumption A6).

Deviation found and fixed during this probe: the committed
pick_query.py from Task 2 called qa_dataset[index] on the FULL
dataset, silently ignoring the <split> CLI argument entirely — 'val'
and 'test' returned identical rows. Fixed to call
qa_dataset.get_subset(split)[index] (STaRKDataset's real split
accessor). Re-verified Task 2's tracer acceptance criteria still pass
post-fix (see raw/tracer-score-one.log, re-recorded against the fix).
